{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('references_provenance.json')); print('REFERENCES:')\nfor ref in r.get('references',[]):\n if any(x in ref.get('title','').lower() for x in ['paired comparison','influence functions','automatic finite','chatbot arena','vote rigg','fivethirtyeight']): print(ref.get('citation_key'),ref.get('title'))\nfor x in ['arena','nba']:\n q=json.load(open('task/resources/final/'+x+'.json'))\n print(x,'rows',len(q['rows']),'players',len(q['participants']),'provenance fields',list(q['provenance'][0]))\np=json.load(open('paper_data.json')); es=p['final_evaluation']['evaluation_evidence']['episodes']\nfor fam,rs in es[0]['solution']['conditional_group_bootstrap'].items():\n print(fam,'count',len(rs),'complete',all(r['complete'] for r in rs),'gain_disagreement min/max',min(r['gain_disagreement'] for r in rs),max(r['gain_disagreement'] for r in rs),'gain_random min/max',min(r['gain_random'] for r in rs),max(r['gain_random'] for r in rs))\nprint('identical bootstrap across episodes?',all(e['solution']['conditional_group_bootstrap']==es[0]['solution']['conditional_group_bootstrap'] for e in es))\nPY\nsed -n '946,962p' task/evaluate_final.py; cat task/requirements.txt; cat results/conclusions.md; ls -la figures\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('references_provenance.json')); print('REFERENCES:')\nfor ref in r.get('references',[]):\n if any(x in ref.get('title','').lower() for x in ['paired comparison','influence functions','automatic finite','chatbot arena','vote rigg','fivethirtyeight']): print(ref.get('citation_key'),ref.get('title'))\nfor x in ['arena','nba']:\n q=json.load(open('task/resources/final/'+x+'.json'))\n print(x,'rows',len(q['rows']),'players',len(q['participants']),'provenance fields',list(q['provenance'][0]))\np=json.load(open('paper_data.json')); es=p['final_evaluation']['evaluation_evidence']['episodes']\nfor fam,rs in es[0]['solution']['conditional_group_bootstrap'].items():\n print(fam,'count',len(rs),'complete',all(r['complete'] for r in rs),'gain_disagreement min/max',min(r['gain_disagreement'] for r in rs),max(r['gain_disagreement'] for r in rs),'gain_random min/max',min(r['gain_random'] for r in rs),max(r['gain_random'] for r in rs))\nprint('identical bootstrap across episodes?',all(e['solution']['conditional_group_bootstrap']==es[0]['solution']['conditional_group_bootstrap'] for e in es))\nPY\nsed -n '946,962p' task/evaluate_final.py; cat task/requirements.txt; cat results/conclusions.md; ls -la figures\"","aggregated_output":"REFERENCES:\nBradley1952RANKAO RANK ANALYSIS OF INCOMPLETE BLOCK DESIGNS THE METHOD OF PAIRED COMPARISONS\nBradley1952RankAO Rank Analysis of Incomplete Block Designs: I. The Method of Paired Comparisons\nDykstra1960RankAO Rank Analysis of Incomplete Block Designs: A Method of Paired Comparisons Employing Unequal Repetitions on Pairs\nBradley1954TheRA The rank analysis of incomplete block designs. II. Additional tables for the method of paired comparisons.\nBradley1955RANKAO RANK ANALYSIS OF INCOMPLETE BLOCK DESIGNS: III. SOME LARGE-SAMPLE RESULTS ON ESTIMATION AND POWER FOR A METHOD OF PAIRED COMPARISONS\nBradley1964CorrigendumTR Corrigendum: The Rank Analysis of Incomplete Block Designs. II. Additional Tables for the Method of Paired Comparisons\nHan2020ExplainingBB Explaining Black Box Predictions and Unveiling Data Artifacts through Influence Functions\nBasu2019SecondOrderGI Second-Order Group Influence Functions for Black-Box Predictions\nBasu2019OnSG On Second-Order Group Influence Functions for Black-Box Predictions\nSaunshi2022UnderstandingIF Understanding Influence Functions and Datamodels via Harmonic Analysis\nZhang2023UnderstandingDG Understanding Deep Gradient Leakage via Inversion Influence Functions\narena rows 38192 players 64 provenance fields ['source_id', 'source_row', 'example_hash', 'content_hashes', 'group']\nnba rows 41418 players 74 provenance fields ['source_id', 'source_row', 'example_hash', 'content_hashes', 'group']\narena count 32 complete True gain_disagreement min/max -0.007936507936507936 -0.0023148148148148147 gain_random min/max -0.0021494708994708994 0.00496031746031746\nnba count 32 complete True gain_disagreement min/max 0.0022213994816734518 0.01949895100580032 gain_random min/max 0.00592373195112921 0.022954461310625694\nidentical bootstrap across episodes? True\n                    controls[1] = True\n            method_masks = {}\n            curves = {}; leader_curves = {}\n            rng = np.random.default_rng(episode['seed'])\n            random_order = rng.permutation(len(canonical))\n            margins = design@clean\n            losses = np.logaddexp(0,margins)-canonical[:,2]*margins\n            disagreement_order = np.lexsort((canonical[:,3],-losses))\n            orders = {'random':random_order,'disagreement':disagreement_order}\n            for method_index,method in enumerate(('random','disagreement','copy','candidate')):\n                method_deadline = reserved_method_deadline(now=time.monotonic(),episode_deadline=deadline,methods_remaining=3-method_index,work_seconds=method_work,cleanup_seconds=.6)\n                with time_bound(method_deadline):\n                    if method=='candidate':\n                        value,previous_token = solve_candidate(call,rows,players,previous_token)\n                        try:\n                            theta,masks = validate_certificate(value,rows,players,clean)\n                        except (TypeError,ValueError,IndexError,OverflowError) as error:\nnumpy==2.2.6\nscipy==1.15.3\nIn the documented anonymous-row, certificate-only candidate interface, optimize contender selection while preserving the clean mean-loss Bradley-Terry fit, supplied ridge, clean Hessian direction, rounded influence ordering, stable row-key tie breaks, and exact nested deletion prefixes. Treat row keys only as identifiers, not missing design or question labels. Retain bounded converged retained-data refits as the selection baseline: recorded aggregate evaluation supports their improvement over the prior clean-Hessian selector in this regime, not a general performance guarantee. Renormalize loss by retained sample size, keep lookahead internal, and distinguish displacement proxies from actual refits. When testing shortlist expansion, preserve existing finalists and bound extra work; retained-curvature screening is an untested lead rather than an established improvement. Measure CPU overhead and external gain because improving the internal selection objective need not improve the external metric. Historical correctness and aggregate gains do not establish completed multi-design scientific evidence or identify the cause of an overall rubric failure. Group dependence, matched-design comparisons, uncertainty analysis, and paper artifacts remain requirements for the broader research study but cannot be claimed from this restricted response channel.\ntotal 8\ndrwx------ 2 agent agent 4096 Nov 17 22:28 .\ndrwx------ 5 agent agent 4096 Nov 17 22:34 ..\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
