{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '138,258p' results/ideas/02_exact_refit_contender_screening/program_1/src/program.py; sed -n '1,75p' results/ideas/03_retained_curvature_shortlist_expansion/program_1/src/IMPLEMENTATION.md; rg -n 'local-memory|local_memory|resolve|symlink' .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py | tail -18; git status --short 2>/dev/null || true\"","aggregated_output":"def shortlist_contenders(screen_records, incumbent_contender, runner_up, limit=6):\n    shortlist = []\n    ordered = [incumbent_contender, runner_up]\n    ordered.extend(record['contender'] for record in sorted(screen_records, key=lambda record: record['score'], reverse=True))\n    for contender in ordered:\n        if contender not in shortlist:\n            shortlist.append(contender)\n        if len(shortlist) >= limit:\n            break\n    return shortlist\n\n\ndef refit_prefix(pair_counts, pair_wins, removed_counts, removed_wins,\n                 regularization, theta):\n    retained_counts = pair_counts - removed_counts\n    retained_wins = pair_wins - removed_wins\n    trial_theta = fit_aggregates(retained_counts, retained_wins, regularization, initial_theta=theta)\n    return trial_theta\n\n\ndef select_contender(rows, theta, hessian, regularization, fractions,\n                     pair_counts, pair_wins):\n    players = len(theta)\n    total_rows = len(rows)\n    ranking = np.lexsort((np.arange(players), -np.round(theta, 8)))\n    leader = int(ranking[0])\n    contenders = ranking[1:]\n    runner_up = int(ranking[1])\n    clean_factor = cho_factor(hessian, lower=True, check_finite=False)\n    inverse_hessian = cho_solve(clean_factor, np.eye(players), check_finite=False)\n    first, second = rows[:, 0].astype(int), rows[:, 1].astype(int)\n    residual = expit(theta[first] - theta[second]) - rows[:, 2]\n    budgets = [int(fraction * len(rows)) for fraction in fractions]\n    best_score = None\n    best_selection = None\n    screen_records = []\n    selection_cache = {}\n    for position, contender_value in enumerate(contenders):\n        contender = int(contender_value)\n        contrast = np.zeros(players)\n        contrast[leader] = 1.0\n        contrast[contender] = -1.0\n        direction = cho_solve(clean_factor, contrast, check_finite=False)\n        influence = residual * (direction[first] - direction[second])\n        order = np.lexsort((rows[:, 3], np.round(influence, 10)))\n        rank_drop_sum = 0\n        target_reversals = 0\n        gap_closure_sum = 0.0\n        original_gap = theta[leader] - theta[contender]\n        for budget in budgets:\n            if budget == 0:\n                continue\n            selected = order[:budget]\n            removed_gradient = np.bincount(first[selected], residual[selected], minlength=players) - np.bincount(second[selected], residual[selected], minlength=players)\n            displacement = np.einsum('ij,j->i', inverse_hessian, removed_gradient + budget * regularization * theta, optimize=False) / (total_rows - budget)\n            predicted_theta = theta + displacement\n            predicted_ranking = np.lexsort((np.arange(players), -np.round(predicted_theta, 8)))\n            rank_drop_sum += int(np.flatnonzero(predicted_ranking == leader)[0])\n            predicted_gap = predicted_theta[leader] - predicted_theta[contender]\n            target_reversals += int(predicted_gap < -1e-8)\n            gap_closure_sum += float(np.clip((original_gap - predicted_gap) / max(original_gap, 1e-8), 0.0, 2.0))\n        score = (rank_drop_sum, target_reversals, gap_closure_sum, -position)\n        selection = (contender, direction, influence, order)\n        screen_records.append({'contender': contender, 'score': score, 'clean_rank': position + 1})\n        selection_cache[contender] = selection\n        kept = {record['contender'] for record in sorted(screen_records, key=lambda record: record['score'], reverse=True)[:6]}\n        kept.add(runner_up)\n        selection_cache = {participant: cached for participant, cached in selection_cache.items() if participant in kept}\n        if best_score is None or score > best_score:\n            best_score = score\n            best_selection = selection\n    incumbent_selection = best_selection\n    incumbent_contender = incumbent_selection[0]\n    shortlist = shortlist_contenders(screen_records, incumbent_contender, runner_up, limit=6)\n    frozen_selections = [selection_cache[contender] for contender in shortlist]\n    clean_ranks = {record['contender']: record['clean_rank'] for record in screen_records}\n    pair_index = first * players + second\n    refit_cache = {(): theta}\n    exact_candidates = []\n    for selection in frozen_selections:\n        contender, direction, influence, order = selection\n        removed_counts = np.zeros_like(pair_counts)\n        removed_wins = np.zeros_like(pair_wins)\n        previous_budget = 0\n        warm_theta = theta\n        rank_drop_sum = 0\n        target_reversals = 0\n        gap_closure_sum = 0.0\n        original_gap = theta[leader] - theta[contender]\n        complete = True\n        for budget in budgets:\n            removed = order[previous_budget:budget]\n            removed_counts += np.bincount(pair_index[removed], minlength=players * players)\n            removed_wins += np.bincount(pair_index[removed], weights=rows[removed, 2], minlength=players * players)\n            previous_budget = budget\n            cache_key = tuple(sorted(order[:budget].tolist()))\n            if cache_key not in refit_cache:\n                try:\n                    refit_cache[cache_key] = refit_prefix(pair_counts, pair_wins, removed_counts,\n                                                         removed_wins, regularization, warm_theta)\n                except (RuntimeError, np.linalg.LinAlgError, ValueError, FloatingPointError):\n                    refit_cache[cache_key] = None\n            trial_theta = refit_cache[cache_key]\n            if trial_theta is None:\n                complete = False\n                break\n            warm_theta = trial_theta\n            trial_ranking = np.lexsort((np.arange(players), -np.round(trial_theta, 8)))\n            rank_drop_sum += int(np.flatnonzero(trial_ranking == leader)[0])\n            trial_gap = trial_theta[leader] - trial_theta[contender]\n            target_reversals += int(trial_gap < -1e-8)\n            gap_closure_sum += float(np.clip((original_gap - trial_gap) / max(original_gap, 1e-8), 0.0, 2.0))\n        if complete:\n            clean_rank = clean_ranks[contender]\n            candidate_score = (rank_drop_sum, target_reversals, gap_closure_sum, -clean_rank)\n            exact_candidates.append({'score': candidate_score, 'selection': selection})\n    if not exact_candidates:\n        return incumbent_selection\n    selected = max(exact_candidates, key=lambda candidate: candidate[\"score\"])\n    return selected['selection']\n\n# Retained-curvature shortlist expansion\n\n## Supported mechanism\n\nThe RPC interface is unchanged. A centered Bradley--Terry fit uses the supplied\nmean-loss ridge penalty, half-win ties, and all observed pairs. Repeated directed\npairs are compressed into sufficient statistics only during fitting; row keys\nand individual outcomes remain intact for influence sorting and export. A\nNewton fit with Cholesky solves and backtracking must satisfy a gradient\ninfinity-norm threshold of `1e-9` before its certificate is exported.\n\nFor every clean nonleader, the program solves the prescribed contrast against\nthe same clean Hessian, computes every row's deletion influence, and orders by\ninfluence rounded to ten decimal places then by the stable row key. Budgets are\nexactly the three required floored row counts. The chosen contender's deletion\nsets are unmodified nested prefixes; there is no iterative order refinement.\n\nThe first-stage contender rule compares clean-Hessian predictions across those\nthree prefixes. For removed set S of size k from n rows, with row gradients g,\nthe predicted parameter displacement is\n\n`H^{-1} (sum_{i in S} g_i + k * regularization * theta) / (n-k)`.\n\nThe penalty correction follows from retaining the contract's mean loss, not a\nsum loss. All predictions use the original fit, original leader, and original\nHessian. They do not refit or retarget after deletions. The selection criterion,\nin lexicographically descending order, is:\n\n1. Sum of predicted original-leader rank drops over the three budgets.\n2. Number of predicted leader-versus-that-contender gaps below `-1e-8`.\n3. Sum of relative target-gap closure, individually clipped to `[0, 2]`, with\n   denominator `max(original_gap, 1e-8)` to handle rounded ranking ties.\n4. Earlier position in the deterministic original ranking.\n\n## Bounded retained-data lookahead\n\nKeep the original at-most-six distinct clean nonleaders: the screening winner first, the\nclean runner-up second (unless already included), and the remaining candidates\nin decreasing screening-score order. Clean certificates are reconstructed on\ndemand from the unchanged clean fit rather than stored for every contender.\nReconstruction always produces the same frozen order. No row swapping,\nadaptive retargeting, or reordering is performed. If these six slots include\nevery nonleader, skip the proxy stage and use the original exact-refit path.\n\nOtherwise seed a deterministic pool with the entire original shortlist, then\nfill in decreasing original screening-score order, capped at 24 contenders.\nFor each pooled contender, incrementally subtract the sufficient statistics of\nits three frozen deletion prefixes. At the original clean theta, calculate the\nretained mean-loss gradient and retained Hessian using the supplied unchanged\nridge. The proxy is one Newton step, `theta - H_retained^{-1} g_retained`,\ncentered to zero mean. It is not a converged fit and has no convergence claim.\nZero budgets reuse clean theta; duplicate budgets reuse the same local proxy.\n\nRank only complete, finite proxy candidates by the same rank-drop, reversal,\ngap-closure, and clean-rank tuple described below. Add at most six outsiders to\nthe original shortlist. Every original finalist remains eligible regardless\nof its proxy quality. Numerical proxy failures exclude that nomination;\nunexpected optional-expansion exceptions restore the original shortlist.\nNeither proxies nor refits ever alter the clean influence ordering.\n\nDirected pair counts and fractional wins are aggregated once and shared by the\nclean fit and all lookahead fits. For each candidate, incrementally subtract\nits frozen prefix's sufficient statistics at the three required budgets. Refit\nthe identical ridge objective, dividing the data loss by the retained row count,\nnot the original count. The supplied ridge coefficient never changes. Scores\nare centered, Newton directions use Cholesky solves, and backtracking accepts\nsufficient objective descent or a roundoff-sized objective change with improved\ngradient residual. Each fit has at most 100 Newton iterations, matching the\nonly accepted `max_iterations` request value. A fit is usable only with finite\nscores and gradient and gradient infinity norm at most `1e-9`.\n\nWarm-start the first positive budget from clean scores and later budgets from\nthe preceding successful refit. Cache scores by the canonical set of removed\nrow positions, including the empty prefix, so identical prefixes reuse their\nfit across candidates and budgets. Duplicate budgets still contribute once\n231:        \"--local-memory-md\",\n400:    local_memory_path = Path(args.local_memory_md)\n404:    _append_text(local_memory_path, _markdown_entry(event), header=LOCAL_MEMORY_HEADERS)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
